{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/864061-the-beleaguered-gm-too-common-of-a-portrayal","id":864061,"title":"The Beleaguered GM: Too Common of a Portrayal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-11T20:02:03-07:00","id":864061,"title":"The Beleaguered GM: Too Common of a Portrayal?","content":"With the Gamers from Dead Gentlemen Productions and various web shows, is the portrayal of the beleaguered possible OCD GM too common of a portrayal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:37:32-07:00","id":864607,"title":"","content":"I have, for a long time, felt that this is part of a larger issue; even when it is &quot;geeks&quot; making stuff that is for or about &quot;geeks&quot;, the stereotypes are too commonly played to.<br /> <br /> So yes, the beleaguered DM gets over-used - as does the portrayal of the player(s) trying to get one over on their DM. The two usually arriving as a pair (or the entire group of players sharing in this trait), explaining the &quot;possible OCD&quot; of the DM and the &quot;aiming to squeeze out an advantage&quot; of each other with the trait of the other being it's cause.<br /> <br /> Though, I think I'll continue to have issues with portrayals of gamer culture right up to the moment that people start asking the opposite questions like &quot;is the portrayal of the easy-going GM more concerned with the group having a good, even if ridiculous, time too common?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T17:33:17-07:00","id":864626,"title":"","content":"The portrayal of the game being GM versus players is so commonplace people believe it to be the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T19:41:21-07:00","id":864672,"title":"","content":"I've been a beleaguered GM many times. Even when I'm enjoying the game, I'll admit I sometimes find the antics of my players tiresome. I don't find beleaguered GMs in fiction to be over-represented or that far off from my own experience.<br /> <br /> Now, the <i>antagonistic</i> GM, paired with asshole players - there's some portrayals we could stand to see less of. Not because they don't happen, but because I don't want that stereotype to spread beyond the gaming community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T23:16:47-07:00","id":864730,"title":"","content":"Art imitates life fellas.<br /> <br /> DMing can get stressful and emotional, especially when you're new at it and playing a complicated game. So, nearly every new D&amp;D group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:18:17-07:00","id":864873,"title":"","content":"DGP is also a comedy group. Meaning the characters they make are supposed to be amusing characters and exaggerated beings rather than &quot;hey this is a typical real world example&quot;<br /> <br /> Very rarely will you find gamers starting boffer fight clubs as a result of boredom (shockingly they're more likely to game), but the writers wanted to make some fight club jokes/references as well as set things up. Even more rarely will you find a game store with a giant near-warehouse back room to store merchandise as I've seen them set up. <br /> <br /> It's why you'll also find variations on the stock comedy characters everywhere else in media, The Bro-Jock, The Ditzy Hot Chick, The Clueless Father, The Nagging Wife, The Creepy Old Man, The Obsessive Gun Collector... all uncommon in Real Life(tm, pat.pend) but very much stock characters in media presentations so you see them a lot, and in comedy they tend to get blown up to greater extremes to emphasize the comedic value of the personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:13:41-07:00","id":868356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/864061-the-beleaguered-gm-too-common-of-a-portrayal?p=864626#post864626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The portrayal of the game being GM versus players is so commonplace people believe it to be the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started a new chronicle recently and we invited a player who had only played in a 3-session game of Pathfinder. I'm struggling every game to make her understand that I'm not against her, I'm with her, trying to create an interesting story.<br /> <br /> She said things like &quot;The GM is God and has absolute authority&quot; and I was just stunned there, trying to imagine what her first game was like, before explaining to her that... <i>no</i>! The ST is as much a player as the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:08:45-07:00","id":868395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/864061-the-beleaguered-gm-too-common-of-a-portrayal?p=868356#post868356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I started a new chronicle recently and we invited a player who had only played in a 3-session game of Pathfinder. I'm struggling every game to make her understand that I'm not against her, I'm with her, trying to create an interesting story.<br /> <br /> She said things like &quot;The GM is God and has absolute authority&quot; and I was just stunned there, trying to imagine what her first game was like, before explaining to her that... <i>no</i>! The ST is as much a player as the others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had the exact opposite problem, going from White Wolf/Indie games to running Pathfinder. Apparently my Pathfinder players were disappointed when I didn't try my best to kill their characters!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:26:14-07:00","id":868408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/864061-the-beleaguered-gm-too-common-of-a-portrayal?p=868395#post868395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I had the exact opposite problem, going from White Wolf/Indie games to running Pathfinder. Apparently my Pathfinder players were disappointed when I didn't try my best to kill their characters!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for experienced players, D&amp;D (except maybe 5th) and Pathfinder are about trying your best to find solutions around problems and create an unbeatable team of adventuring. So yeah I can say I was bored when my ST never killed us even when we just clearly acted stupid.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D is like a Rogue-Like RPG. YMMV, but there's a reason why it's fun even if you play the same scenario 5 times","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:21:26-07:00","id":894314,"title":"","content":"I often GM because I want to do *less* work, not more. Burning Wheel, for example, requires significantly more effort for me on the player side of things. That said, I don't play D&amp;D very often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T01:01:02-07:00","id":894606,"title":"","content":"I find that the portrayal of the beleaguered GM is a stereotype that is based in a bit of fact though. No matter how I may personally GM/ST, I do find that there will typically be at least one or two players in every group who, thanks to previous GMs, will see the GM position as an adversarial one. They'll be the one's asking to play some obscure race with an obscure class to get some kind of Killer McKillerton style character who can slay anything in one hit because of a missed comma in a text box somewhere.<br /> <br /> Luckily in WoD I find this to not really be a problem. Let Killer have his moment in combats, then throw some social scenes at him, or make him need to figure out how to get inside a safe without killing anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not denigrating Pathfinder, I love me some hack and slash, but I find such players more of a problem in a more traditional RPG. If there are a group of four players and only one wants his super killer power fantasy, they tend to screw up encounter design. Say you design a boss fight with Killer in mind, if he's away, its going to be too difficult. However, if you design a &quot;balanced&quot; encounter and he's there, he's going to make it a cakewalk and give no one else a chance to shine.<br /> <br /> Hence, yeah, with the extra stress of trying to cater to such things, I can definitely feel like a beleaguered GM :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 05-20-2016, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:17:30-07:00","id":895227,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there are a lot of tired GMs out there. Unless you have a rare, awesome group, the GM is gonna put forward more effort than anyone else at the table (they have to learn and then teach the rules and setting, come up with a story idea, and improvise plausible reactions for literally any possible action, all while playing multiple roles - and in my experience, likely hosting the game as well!) and probably get less out of it. I burnt out trying to run games for my friends and haven't bothered finding a new group because it just largely isn't worth the effort; you're not gonna find three to five nerds who are also great improv actors and interested in the same niche ideas as you - and if you do, there's no way in hell they all have the same chunk of three to six hours off every single week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}